unt needed for the next step        * `userData` - generic blob used to pass extra data"}},"constructor":{"params":{"_creditManager":"Credit manager address","_vault":"Balancer vault address"}},"exitPool(bytes32,address,address,(address[],uint256[],bytes,bool))":{"details":"`sender` and `recipient` are ignored, since they are always set to the CA address","params":{"poolId":"ID of the pool to withdraw from","request":"A struct containing data for executing a withdrawal:        * `assets` - Array of all assets in the pool        * `minAmountsOut` - The minimal amounts to receive for each asset        * `userData` - a blob encoding the type of deposit and additional parameters          (see https://dev.balancer.fi/resources/joins-and-exits/pool-exits#userdata for more info)        * `toInternalBalance` - whether to use internal balances for assets          (ignored as the adapter does not use internal balances)"}},"exitPoolSingleAsset(bytes32,address,uint256,uint256)":{"params":{"amountIn":"Amount of BPT to burn","assetOut":"Asset to withdraw","minAmountOut":"Minimal amount of asset to receive","poolId":"ID of the pool to withdraw from"}},"exitPoolSingleAssetDiff(bytes32,address,uint256,uint256)":{"params":{"assetOut":"Asset to withdraw","leftoverAmount":"Amount of pool token to keep on the account","minRateRAY":"Minimal exchange rate of BPT to assetOut, scaled by 1e27","poolId":"ID of the pool to withdraw from"}},"joinPool(bytes32,address,address,(address[],uint256[],bytes,bool))":{"details":"`sender` and `recipient` are ignored, since they are always set to the CA addressThe function reverts if poolId status is not ALLOWED","params":{"poolId":"ID of the pool to deposit into","request":"A struct containing data for executing a deposit:        * `assets` - Array of assets in the pool        * `maxAmountsIn` - Array of maximal amounts to be spent for each asset        * `userData` - a blob encoding the type of deposit and additional parameters          (see https://dev.balancer.fi/resources/joins-and-exits/pool-joins#userdata for more info)        * `fromInternalBalance` - whether to use internal balances for assets          (ignored as the adapter does not use internal balances)"}},"joinPoolSingleAsset(bytes32,address,uint256,uint256)":{"details":"The function reverts if poolId status is not ALLOWED","params":{"amountIn":"Amount of asset to deposit","assetIn":"Asset to deposit","minAmountOut":"The minimal amount of BPT to receive","poolId":"ID of the pool to deposit into"}},"joinPoolSingleAssetDiff(bytes32,address,uint256,uint256)":{"details":"The function reverts if poolId status is not ALLOWED","params":{"assetIn":"Asset to deposit","leftoverAmount":"Amount of underlying to keep on the account","minRateRAY":"The minimal exchange rate of assetIn to BPT, scaled by 1e27","poolId":"ID of the pool to deposit into"}},"swap((bytes32,uint8,address,address,uint256,bytes),(address,bool,address,bool),uint256,uint256)":{"details":"`fundManagement` param from the original interface is ignored, as the adapter does not use internal balances and       only has one sender/recipientThe function reverts if the poolId status is not ALLOWED or SWAP_ONLY","params":{"deadline":"The latest timestamp at which the swap would be executed","limit":"The minimal amount of `assetOut` to receive or maximal amount of `assetIn` to spend (depending on `kind`)","singleSwap":"Struct containing swap parameters        * `poolId` - ID of the pool to perform a swap in        * `kind` - type of swap (GIVEN IN / GIVEN OUT)        * `assetIn` - asset to send        * `assetOut` - asset to receive        * `amount` - amount of input asset to send (for GIVEN IN) or output asset to receive (for GIVEN OUT)        * `userData` - generic blob used to pass extra data"}},"swapDiff((bytes32,uint256,address,address,bytes),uint256,uint256)":{"details":"The function reverts if the poolId status is not ALLOWED or SWAP_ONLY","params":{"deadline":"The latest timestamp at which the swap would be executed","limitRateRAY":"The minimal resulting exchange rate of assetOut to assetIn, scaled by 1e27","singleSwapDiff":"Struct containing swap parameters        * `poolId` - ID of the pool to perform a swap in        * `leftoverAmount` - amount of assetIn to leave after operation        * `assetIn` - asset to send        * `assetOut` - asset to receive        * `userData` - additional generic blob used to pass extra data"}}},"title":"Balancer V2 Vault adapter","version":1},"userdoc":{"errors":{"CallerNotConfiguratorException()":[{"notice":"Thrown on attempting to call an access restricted function not as configurator"}],"CallerNotCreditFacadeException()":[{"notice":"Thrown on attempting to call an access restricted function not as credit facade"}],"PoolNotSupportedException()":[{"notice":"Thrown when attempting to swap or change liqudity in the pool that is not supported for that action"}],"ZeroAddressException()":[{"notice":"Thrown on attempting to set an important address to zero address"}]},"events":{"SetPoolStatus(bytes32,uint8)":{"notice":"Emitted when new status is set for a pool with given ID"}},"kind":"user","methods":{"acl()":{"notice":"ACL contract address"},"addressProvider()":{"notice":"Address provider contract"},"batchSwap(uint8,(bytes32,uint256,uint256,uint256,bytes)[],address[],(address,bool,address,bool),int256[],uint256)":{"notice":"Performs a multi-hop swap through several Balancer pools"},"constructor":{"notice":"Constructor"},"creditManager()":{"notice":"Credit manager the adapter is connected to"},"exitPool(bytes32,address,address,(address[],uint256[],bytes,bool))":{"notice":"Withdraws liquidity from a Balancer pool, burning BPT and receiving assets"},"exitPoolSingleAsset(bytes32,address,uint256,uint256)":{"notice":"Withdraws liquidity from a Balancer pool, burning BPT and receiving a single asset"},"exitPoolSingleAssetDiff(bytes32,address,uint256,uint256)":{"notice":"Withdraws all liquidity from a Balancer pool except the specified 